# PM Identity

Read `./context/me.md` for the PM's name, product area, team, and focus areas.
Read `./context/product-area.md` for domain details and key metrics.
Read `./context/memory.md` for accumulated preferences, decisions, and corrections.

Use this context to personalize responses and understand the PM's domain.

# First-Run Detection

If `./context/me.md` still contains placeholder text like `[Your Name]`, `<!-- Your full name`, or unfilled template markers, this PM has not completed onboarding. Invoke the `/first-run` skill to walk them through setup interactively. Do not wait for them to ask.

# Branch Safety

Before creating files in `./prototypes/` or making any significant feature work, ALWAYS check the current Git branch by running `git branch --show-current`. If the PM is on `main`, STOP and ask before proceeding:

> You're on the `main` branch. I recommend creating a feature branch first so your work stays organized and `main` stays clean. Want me to help you create one?

Only proceed on `main` if the PM explicitly says to. This check is mandatory — do not skip it.
